# origin/main behaviour (baseline per maintainer decision 6)
# Generated by TestLegacyLogsParser (pkg/characterization); regenerate with -update. Do not edit.
# Operation: FileLogsRepository.GetLogs (pkg/adapter/secondary/file_logs_repository.go:32-71), on lines written by pkg/logging and host.RunLog, run in a child process
# Writers: every line in hardn's log comes through pkg/logging's logger, log.LstdFlags, so "DATE TIME LEVEL: message" (logging.go:46, :78-133). The run log (runlog.go:47-69) has no writer of its own: revertFileLog sends each of its lines to LogFileOnly, so they are INFO lines (confirm.go:158-163). LogFileOnly's lines say INFO whatever they report.
# KNOWN-DEFECT: GetLogs splits on the first two spaces, for "TIME LEVEL: MESSAGE" (file_logs_repository.go:51-57), a format hardn does not write: Time holds the date, Level the time, and Message the level and the message. No entry has a level.
# KNOWN-DEFECT: A line that is not one of the logger's, the second line of a message with a line break, is taken as an entry if it has three words and dropped if it has fewer (:53).
# KNOWN-DEFECT: A line over bufio.Scanner's 64 KiB limit ends the read with no error: scanner.Err is not checked (:47-70), so it and everything after it are lost.
# NOTE: No live path calls GetLogs: the callers below are the two forwarding methods, and LogsManager.GetLogs has no caller. pkg/domain/service/logs_service_test.go tests it on a mock repository. The screen and -p print the raw file. pkg/utils.PrintLogs (utils.go:117) has no caller either.
# NOTE: No V-number holds these; plan slice 1's row names the broken parser.
# The date and time are masked. The long line is shortened here; the entries show what survives it.
